    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CASH BUYERS ONLY\r\n\r\nUniquely and unlike other official holiday homes in the area. Meath County Council have changed the zoning area map to residential. The successful purchaser must be a cash buyer as mortgages are not currently available. \r\n \r\nAn excellent opportunity to acquire a charming 3-bedroom detached bungalow ideally positioned within a small development of detached bungalow homes and occupying an enviable end-of-development position, this delightful home enjoys exceptional privacy and tranquility, with open farmland bordering both the rear and side of the property, creating a peaceful setting rarely found so close to local amenities.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 70 SQM / 753 SQFT, this property is full of charm and character and offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation throughout.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a welcoming entrance hall, a cozy yet spacious open-plan living/dining area featuring a stove and sliding doors opening onto the garden area, a galley-style kitchen, guest WC, two double bedrooms, one single bedroom, and a main bathroom complete with a shower cubicle and electric shower.\r\n\r\nThe property benefits from gas-fired central heating and communal parking within the development.\r\n\r\nOne of the standout features of this home is its exceptionally private setting. Located at the very end of the development which offers a wonderful sense of peace and seclusion.\r\n\r\nTransport \r\n* Bus Éireann and Matthews Bus stops are only a few minutes’ walk away and services Dublin, Drogheda and Laytown. \r\n* Laytown Train Station (Park & Ride) with frequent services to Dublin Connolly and beyond \r\n* Easy access to the M1 motorway – Dublin City Centre, Dundalk and Airport within easy reach \r\n\r\nHealthcare \r\n* HSE Primary Health Centre in the Bettystown Town Centre. \r\n* Our Lady of Lourdes Hospital, Drogheda.\r\n\r\nDining & Leisure\r\nA vibrant local food scene including Navy Café, The Village Hotel, Duende and Matt the Thrasher Gastropub, along with a wide selection of coffee shops, takeaways and traditional pubs. \r\n\r\nSports & Recreation \r\n* Laytown & Bettystown Golf Club – renowned 18-hole links course across the road. \r\n* Excellent range of sporting clubs including GAA, rugby, football, athletics, boxing and more. \r\n* Scenic coastal and Boyne Valley walking and cycling routes. \r\n\r\nShopping & Services \r\n* Nearby retail options include Tesco, LIDL, ALDI, Dunnes Stores, SuperValu, Centra, MACE and Mr Price. \r\n* South Gate & Scotch Hall shopping centres are approximately a 10-minute drive away. \r\n* Drogheda Town Centre just 15 minutes away for extensive shopping. \r\n\r\nExcellent selection of pre-primary, primary and secondary schools. Post office, pharmacies, veterinary clinics, butcher, Integral Fitness Club with heated swimming pool and local services. Petrol station only a 5 -minute drive away.\r\n\r\nPlease note that the photos are historic and the details and photos are for guidance purposes only.  \r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
